4. Wrapped the component with RouterContext.Provider using the mock router object

This should fix the "jest is not defined" error while still maintaining the same functionality. The component will still receive the router context it needs, but now it's provided through Next.js's built-in RouterContext provider instead of Jest mocks.

The TagPageComponent will render exactly as it does in the main application, just with a mocked router context which is necessary for preview environments. No modifications have been made to the actual TagPageComponent itself.

